# iterative thinking — a refused proposal is followed, in the same thinking, by another try
#
# A pineal gland of 1 gives one retry (ThinkingIterationsStat) and no doubt (DoubtStat needs 2).
# The goal draw is pinned to examine and the first means to Knack, which the coded willingness rule
# refuses ("I want to act, not to stand and observe"). With a retry left the same mind thinks again:
# examine comes back at once, since other means are able to carry it out, and it is carried out by
# one of those — Butchery, at seed 42 — which is not asked whether it would rather not. One thinking,
# one button.
# Without the retry (pineal_gland=0, see thinking_refused_goal_per_mind.cli) the thinking ends on the
# refusal and it is the next thinking that reaches examine.
#
# --means-only knack cannot hold on the retry, whose pool has Knack crossed off; that miss is the
# point, hence allow-flag-miss.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Crown" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Giant Tree" --grant-mm knack,woodcraft,scientific_research --means-only knack --organs pineal_gland=1

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal examine
advance 12 180

# Think with Ripelore: Knack refuses, the mind acknowledges it and tries again, and the retry
# reaches the button.
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
expect I want to act, not to stand and
expect That will not do, and I think again
expect another way
expect ] examine the test giant tree closely
expect-not But is it truly wise

allow-flag-miss --goal-only
allow-flag-miss --means-only
quit
